BEHAVIOR sha256

DESCRIPTION
  SHA-256 (FIPS 180-4) of the first len bytes of data. Writes the 32-byte
  big-endian digest. Pads per the standard (0x80, zeros, then the 64-bit
  big-endian bit length), and processes 64-byte blocks. Examples:
  sha256("") = e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855;
  sha256("abc") = ba7816bf8f01cfea414140de5dae2223b00361a396177a9cb410ff61f20015ad.
  K constants and the message schedule W live in a scratch buffer; all
  arithmetic is 32-bit (masked with M = 4294967295 = 0xFFFFFFFF). data is
  capped at 65536 bytes, so the padded message fits in the buffer.

CONTRACT
  INPUT data bytes 65536
  INPUT len int 8
  OUTPUT digest bytes 32
  GUARANTEES writes_output

HASH b5957c49

IMPLEMENTATION
  M = 4294967295
  lenv = LOAD len 8
  buf = ALLOC 66560 bytes

